The test creates one `Faker()` instance, seeds it with `seed_instance(777777)`, then makes four provider calls before `doi()`. From `Generator.seed_instance`, those calls all advance the same instance-specific `random` object used later by `doi()`. In `faker/providers/doi/__init__.py`, `doi()` returns `f"{prefix}.{registrant}/{suffix}"` where `prefix` is `"10"` (2 chars), `"."` adds 1, `"/"` adds 1, and `suffix` from `bothify("?#?#?##").lower()` is always 7 chars. For this seeded call sequence, the generated `registrant` has 8 digits, so the total length is `2 + 1 + 8 + 1 + 7 = 19`.

## Answer
{"doi_char_len":19}
